{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Hallelujah.</b> This psalm is very esteemed and it contains deep secrets. Now it begins to speak of two worlds: the first, the upper world, which is the broad and great world; and afterward it mentions the lower world, which is like a point in the thought of one contemplating a great circle. And it begins to say: הללויה, 'You from the heavens, praise Him' — in the heights. The meaning is: you who dwell in the exalted heavens, and they are the heaven of heavens."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 148, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:43:05.015746847Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}